    "focal_pair": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 1 USER]\ne001\tMy brother Tomas and I have been digitizing boxes of family photographs, letters, and recordings.\ne002\tA local cultural center offered us a small exhibition next spring about migration into the neighborhood.\ne003\tTomas wants to accept because a public date would help us finish and the material could mean something beyond our family.\ne004\tI want the archive organized first.\ne005\tRight now captions are incomplete, some stories conflict, and I worry the exhibition will turn a complicated family history into a clean public narrative.\n[Turn 1 ASSISTANT]\ne006\tThe exhibition could create momentum and public value, but it also changes the purpose of the archive from preservation to interpretation.\ne007\tYou may not need to finish the whole archive before exhibiting a carefully bounded selection.\ne008\tThe first question is whether you and Tomas agree on what the exhibition is allowed to claim, especially where accounts conflict.\ne009\tA date can help with completion while also pressuring you to resolve ambiguity cosmetically.",
